       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 2000 mg three times daily comes to 6 g/day, which is above the usual adult maximum of 4 g/day. That is a risk of hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function. The 4 g/day limit is lower, often 3 g/day, in many hospital protocols. A 70 kg patient doesn't change that limit.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3 g/day), a common standard order.\n- **1000 mg PO four times daily** (4 g/day), the maximum.\n- **650 mg PO four times daily** (2.6 g/day), a lower-dose option.\n- **2000 mg PO three times daily**, if you really mean it. Tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first.\n\nWhich would you like? If 2000 mg was a typo, I can enter one of the options above right away."
      }
